@host = http://localhost:9003
@gateway = http://localhost:8080

### NOTE: adding/updating items requires Restaurant Service to be registered
### with Eureka (service-registry running, restaurant-service up) and to
### expose GET /restaurants/menu/{itemId} -> { "id", "name", "price", "available" }.
### Cart Service resolves restaurant-service's address from Eureka directly -
### it does not go through the API Gateway for this call.
### See service/RestaurantClient.java for the exact contract this service calls.

### get my cart (auto-creates an empty one in the response if none exists yet)
GET {{host}}/carts/user-1

### add an item to the cart - only itemId/quantity are trusted from the client,
### name/price/availability are fetched live from Restaurant Service
POST {{host}}/carts/user-1/items
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "itemId": "item-1",
  "quantity": 2
}

### add another item
POST {{host}}/carts/user-1/items
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "itemId": "item-2",
  "quantity": 1
}

### add more of an item already in the cart (quantity accumulates, price/name refreshed)
POST {{host}}/carts/user-1/items
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "itemId": "item-1",
  "quantity": 1
}

### update an item's quantity (re-checks price/availability with Restaurant Service)
PUT {{host}}/carts/user-1/items/item-1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "quantity": 3
}

### setting quantity to 0 removes the item (no Restaurant Service call needed)
PUT {{host}}/carts/user-1/items/item-1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "quantity": 0
}

### remove an item directly
DELETE {{host}}/carts/user-1/items/item-2

### apply a coupon code (held only - Order Service validates/applies it at checkout)
PUT {{host}}/carts/user-1/coupon
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "couponCode": "WELCOME10"
}

### remove the coupon
DELETE {{host}}/carts/user-1/coupon

### checkout - publishes a CartCheckedOut event to RabbitMQ for Order Service,
### then clears the cart
POST {{host}}/carts/user-1/checkout

### clear the whole cart manually (e.g. user abandons it)
DELETE {{host}}/carts/user-1

### same get-cart call through the API Gateway
GET {{gateway}}/carts/user-1
